    "narrative": "The lineup for Ghost Ride the WHIP today leans heavily into favorable matchups against vulnerable arms, with **Corbin Carroll** standing out as the unequivocal anchor of our offensive attack. With a massive efficiency score of 85.93, **Corbin Carroll** faces Feltner in a prime spot to exploit a 4.96 xERA matchup; his elite sprint speed makes him the primary engine for our category scarcity needs, and hitting second provides the optimal runway to rack up Runs. **Mickey Moniak** serves as a high-upside secondary play at 75.98, benefiting from a robust +14% platoon edge against Kelly, while **Gabriel Moreno** anchors the core with a 71.16 score, capitalizing on the same soft matchup against Feltner to provide stability in both AVG and RBI.\n\nWe are navigating a few marginal spots where the data suggests caution. **Austin Riley** sits at 58.01, teetering on the edge of our efficiency floor; while he draws a solid 4.62 xERA pitcher in Thornton, his placement at the bottom of the order and the defensive skill of the opposition suppress his daily value. **Max Muncy** represents our most precarious start at 43.71; while he benefits from a positive park factor, the combination of a lower-tier lineup spot and a negative platoon differential against Rasmussen makes him a candidate to be swapped if any late-breaking news surfaces. The most notable exclusion today is the depth of our bench, as **Jose Caballero** remains sidelined, forcing us to lean on the existing starters despite the thin margin between **Cole Young** (47.70) and a potential replacement. With no weather-related delays on the horizon, the focus remains on leveraging the speed of **Corbin Carroll** and **Brice Turang** to widen the gap in our most contested category.",
